 ### Labels 

 A Label in Kubernetes is a key-value pair attached to a resource such as a Pod, Deployment, or Service. Labels help you identify, group, and organize resources.

 Example : app=nginx

 app = Key

 nginx = values

 57.Syntax : kubectl label <resorce-type> <resource-name> <key>=<value> -n <namespace>

   Example : kubectl run label-pod --image=nginx:1.27 -n dev-lab

58. To view the labels
  
   Syntax :  kubectl get pods -n <namespace> --show-labels

   Example : kubectl get pods -n dev-lab --show-labels

59.  Add new label to the existing pod {Envronment label}

    Syntax : kubectl label <resource-type> <resource-name> <key>=<value> -n <namespace>

    Exaample : kubect label pod label-pod env=dev -n dev-lab

    for deployment :

    kubectl label deployment web-app env=dev -n dev-lab`  


    run=label-pod  → identifies how the Pod was created
    env=dev  → says this Pod belongs to the development environment

